                <pb facs="1086" n="991" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg991"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3394/239: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Neville</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-04T10:00:00+09:00">September 4, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 4—12:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>177. Department’s 225, August 11, 4 p.m. via Shanghai. Japanese Foreign Office by
                    note dated yesterday has informed the Embassy that the Japanese Government has
                    no objection to the proposed visit of the <hi rendition="#italic">Gold Star</hi>
                    at Miike but regrets it cannot give consent to proposed visits at Truk, Palau
                    and Saipan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Neville</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
